  "caveats": [
    "Instrumented stock versus instrumented PR47 at one exact upstream app commit on one Mac and built-in 120Hz display; four valid runs per condition, not independent per-frame replicates.",
    "Absolute-schedule synthetic GPUI packet replay; it does not reproduce every physical trackpad/momentum path. Primary cadence covers fixed sustained-motion source windows, 4.601196s/run; tails/full-phase results are separate.",
    "Foreground readiness is conditional; two fixed startup focus failures were retained, one pilot and one main-series attempt, with no proven PR47 attribution.",
    "Positive unique drawable presentedTime is the measured output. Lower GPU energy with fewer presentations does not establish energy efficiency at equal output. CPU activity increased in all four adjacent pairs.",
    "GPU Energy is the whole-device IOReport Energy Model in nJ, not app-specific, wall/socket, battery discharge, or total-system watts. WindowServer and other desktop workloads share it.",
    "Per-process IOKit accumulatedGPUTime is accounted execution time, not GPU utilization or peak load. GPU command-buffer elapsed durations are different counters.",
    "Telemetry windows are broader than primary cadence cores; do not divide full-window energy by core-only frame count.",
    "Observer parent CPU was 1.251\u20131.307 percent of one core; its children CPU includes the app and must not be added as observer overhead.",
    "Idle-after app GPU was essentially zero, while whole-device energy and WindowServer activity remained variable; no pure per-app watts can be inferred from idle subtraction.",
    "Recorded display/power/geometry/thermal controls and the runner game/compiler guard matched. They cannot exclude every background GPU consumer; WindowServer is a shared compositor.",
    "A zero/not-presented drawable callback means that particular submitted drawable was not positively reported displayed. It is retained as an outcome and must not automatically be described as a perceptible dropped animation frame.",
    "GPU performance-state residency and driver utilization are separate from shader occupancy or thermal/power saturation. This experiment does not establish saturation."
  ]
